<title>FRANCE: Jan-Sept Paris airport import traffic up one pct.</title>
<headline>Jan-Sept Paris airport import traffic up one pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>January-September 1996 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 383,408 tonnes, an increase of one percent on the same period last year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>Traffic from  North America, the principal region of origin for ADP imports, rose by 3.5 percent to 135,601 tonnes in contrast to Far East-originating cargo which fell 0.6 percent to 83,688 tonnes.</p>
<p>Import traffic from sub-Saharan Africa rose by 9.4 percent on the first nine months of 1995 to 39,408 tonnes.</p>
<p>Import traffic, by region, in tonnes with percentage change on January- September 1995, was as follows:</p>
<p>    Domestic		  22,330    down  13.7</p>
<p>    European Union	  45,505    up     6.1</p>
<p>    Non-EU Europe	    8,230    up     3.6</p>
<p>    North Africa	     7,705    down  11.9</p>
<p>    Sub-Saharan Africa    39,408    up     9.4</p>
<p>    North America	  135,601    up     3.5</p>
<p>    French territories     9,479    down   3.9</p>
<p>    Latin America	   13,499    down   5.2</p>
<p>    Middle East	     17,963    down   4.2</p>
<p>    Far East		  83,688    down   0.6</p>
<p>    Total		    383,408    up     1.0</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
